cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or the model, please cite the paper (preferred-citation below)."
type: software
title: "Perpetual Preferred Against Bitcoin Structural Credit Model"
abstract: "Reference implementation and test vectors for the paper Perpetual Preferred Equity Against Bitcoin: A Closed-Form Structural Credit Model (Fairbanks, 2026). Three pure standard-library Python functions: the closed-form price equation, the Distance-to-Coverage-Breach (DCB), and the drift-free breach probability. The checks reproduce the four test vectors of Appendix D.5 and all 231 numeric cells of Tables 1 through 5 and Table C.1."
